\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Insertions when the kernel has no inverse}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The paired determinant in \ref{fdip-00TL} exists for every kernel.
The complex source identity in \ref{fdip-00IV} also records insertions,
but writes them using an inverse kernel. What finite source
polynomial records the same coefficients over a ring, and what
does it retain when that inverse is unavailable?}
